\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Is there a real homogeneous hyperbolic polynomial whose closed cone has an exact finite semidefinite lift but is not itself the positive-semidefinite locus of any affine symmetric pencil in its original variables? Auxiliary variables are allowed for the lift but forbidden in the latter representation.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Is there a real homogeneous hyperbolic polynomial whose closed cone has an exact finite semidefinite lift but is not itself the positive-semidefinite locus of any affine symmetric pencil in its original variables? Auxiliary variables are allowed for the lift but forbidden in the latter representation.

